{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Goran Dragić (born 6 May 1986) is a Slovenian professional basketball for the Miami Heat of the National Basketball Association (NBA).","title":"Goran Dragić"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He plays at both the point guard and shooting guard positions.","title":"Goran Dragić"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He played professional basketball in Slovenia and Spain before entering the NBA in 2008.","title":"Goran Dragić"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Dragić has played for the Phoenix Suns twice, the Houston Rockets, and the Miami Heat.","title":"Goran Dragić"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" He was an All-NBA Third Team selection and the NBA Most Improved Player in 2014.","title":"Goran Dragić"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Damond L. Williams (born October 10, 1980) is an American professional basketball player in the International Basketball Federation (FIBA) Asia League.","title":"Damond Williams"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Williams, who is 6'6", is known for his versatility as a combo guard, effective at playing both point guard and shooting guard positions.","title":"Damond Williams"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He led his team through a perfect season in the Syrian Premier League and Syrian League Cup in the 2009 season.","title":"Damond Williams"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" In 2009 Damond was voted the best shooting guard of the 20th Dubai International Basketball Tournament.","title":"Damond Williams"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Damond is also Founder of the Chicago Basketball Academy a private non-sectarian coeducational high school focused on academic and athletic excellence in the field of basketball.","title":"Damond Williams"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The shooting guard (SG), also known as the two or off guard, is one of the five positions in a regulation basketball game.","title":"Shooting guard"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" A shooting guard's main objective is to score points for his team.","title":"Shooting guard"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Some teams ask their shooting guards to bring up the ball as well; these players are known colloquially as combo guards.","title":"Shooting guard"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Kobe Bryant, for example, as a shooting guard was as good a playmaker as he was a scorer; other examples of combo guards are Dwyane Wade, Allen Iverson, James Harden, Manu Ginóbili, Jamal Crawford, Randy Foye and Jason Terry.","title":"Shooting guard"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" A player who can switch between playing shooting guard and small forward is known as a swingman.","title":"Shooting guard"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Notable swing men (also known as wing players) include Jimmy Butler, Tracy McGrady, Vince Carter, Joe Johnson, Andre Iguodala, Andrew Wiggins, Evan Turner and Tyreke Evans.","title":"Shooting guard"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" In the NBA, shooting guards usually range from 6' 4" (1.93 m) to 6' 7" (2.01 m) and 5' 9" (1.75 m) to 6' 0" (1.83 m) in the WNBA.","title":"Shooting guard"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Igor Rakočević (; born March 29, 1978) is a retired Serbian professional basketball player.","title":"Igor Rakočević"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He is 1.94 m (6 ft 4 ½ in) tall.","title":"Igor Rakočević"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" A two-time All-EuroLeague Team member and three-time Alphonso Ford Trophy winner, he played at both the point guard and shooting guard positions, but spent the vast majority of his career playing as a shooting guard.","title":"Igor Rakočević"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He is the son of Serbian former basketball player Goran Rakočević, who played as a point guard for Crvena zvezda.","title":"Igor Rakočević"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Since February 2015, he has been a vice-president of the Basketball Federation of Serbia, in charge of men’s basketball.","title":"Igor Rakočević"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Lucio Redivo (born February 14, 1994) is an Argentinian professional basketball player who currently plays for Bilbao Basket in the Liga ACB.","title":"Lucio Redivo"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He can play at both the point guard and shooting guard positions, with shooting guard being his main position.","title":"Lucio Redivo"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Ramon "Dale" Singson (born December 2, 1975) is a Filipino former professional basketball player.","title":"Dale Singson"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He last played for the Powerade Tigers in the Philippine Basketball Association.","title":"Dale Singson"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He plays the Point Guard and Shooting Guard positions.","title":"Dale Singson"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He was directly hired by the Shell Turbo Chargers from the MBA in 2000.","title":"Dale Singson"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" He was known as a scorer who can play both guard positions.","title":"Dale Singson"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Miami Heat
