{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Sophie Lara Winkleman (born 5 August 1980) is an English actress.","title":"Sophie Winkleman"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" As the wife of Lord Frederick Windsor, son of Queen Elizabeth II's first cousin Prince Michael of Kent, she is formally referred to as Lady Frederick Windsor, but continues to use her maiden name in her professional career.","title":"Sophie Winkleman"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"ElvenQuest is a comic fantasy broadcast on BBC Radio 4 by Anil Gupta and Richard Pinto, and starring Stephen Mangan, Alistair McGowan, Darren Boyd, Kevin Eldon, Sophie Winkleman and Dave Lamb.","title":"ElvenQuest"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The series takes place in the world of Lower Earth, a parody of Middle-earth from "The Lord of the Rings" by J. R. R. Tolkien.","title":"ElvenQuest"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" In Lower Earth, a band of warriors go forth to search for a mythical sword to save Lower Earth from the evil Lord Darkness (played by McGowan).","title":"ElvenQuest"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" In order to do so, they must find "The Chosen One" who will save Lower Earth.","title":"ElvenQuest"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The Chosen One is Amis, a dog in the real world which belongs to a fantasy novelist called Sam Porter (played by Mangan).","title":"ElvenQuest"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The first series was broadcast from 29 March to 3 June 2009 and the second from 18 November 2010.","title":"ElvenQuest"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" The third series began broadcasting from 17 October 2011.","title":"ElvenQuest"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" The fourth series began broadcasting 12 February 2013.","title":"ElvenQuest"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Comic fantasy is a subgenre of fantasy that is primarily humorous in intent and tone.","title":"Comic fantasy"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Usually set in imaginary worlds, comic fantasy often includes puns on and parodies of other works of fantasy.","title":"Comic fantasy"},{"sentence_id":2,"text"